{"call_id":"call_zQMGsbPoA1Oa5JkGLDF3qAzN","process_id":"78128","turn_id":"019ca307-fce8-7ee3-9b24-8e9326fe34a0","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task get @01KJDQ15 --json"],"cwd":"/workspace","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task get @01KJDQ15 --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1513YJA4PKRTA8CZDE4P\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"kspec task set --priority accepts numbers (1-5) but all documentation, conventions, and plan documen\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec task set --priority` and `kspec task add --priority` only accept raw numbers (1-5), but all documentation, conventions, and plan documents use P1/P2/P3 notation. The error message says 'Priority must be a number between 1 and 5' which is confusing when P-notation is used everywhere else. **Where**: `src/cli/validators.ts` — the `parseIntOption()` function (line 36-64) is used for priority parsing. It calls `Number(value)` which rejects `P1` etc. The priority option is defined in `src/cli/commands/task.ts` at lines 608, 827. The `parseIntOption` is called at lines 287-296 (task set) and 759-767 (task add). **How**: Create a `parsePriority()` wrapper function in `src/cli/validators.ts` that first normalizes P-notation before calling `parseIntOption()`. Implementation: strip a leading case-insensitive `P` prefix if present (`value.replace(/^[Pp]/, '')`), then delegate to `parseIntOption()`. Replace all `parseIntOption(options.priority, { min: 1, max: 5, name: 'Priority' })` calls in `task.ts` with `parsePriority(options.priority)`. Update the option description from 'Priority (1-5)' to 'Priority (1-5 or P1-P5)'. Update the error message to mention both formats. **Done when**: (1) `kspec task set @ref --priority P1` works and sets priority to 1. (2) `kspec task add --priority p3` works (case-insensitive). (3) `kspec task set @ref --priority 2` still works (backward compatible). (4) Invalid values like `P6`, `Px`, `0` are rejected with a clear error mentioning both formats. (5) Tests in `tests/cli-validators.test.ts` cover both formats. (6) CLI help text shows accepted format.\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@batch-exec\",\n  \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"session_id\": \"01KJHCVA63NR1MQFKHV6JN8QRE\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:32:52.387Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-02-28T06:50:50.347Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-02-28T06:53:37.898Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJHGC0GS6CFYHAAVGGQ4YPYY\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T06:53:25.914Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented priority parsing parity for task add/set: added parsePriority() to accept numeric (1-5) and P-notation (P1-P5, case-insensitive), updated task CLI option help text to document both formats, and added regression coverage in tests/cli-validators.test.ts plus integration tests for task add/set with P-notation and invalid Px guidance. Verification: npm test -- --run tests/cli-validators.test.ts tests/integration.test.ts (198 passed).\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJHGFXY696XZY0JF0HXBRPMV\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-28T06:55:34.342Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"[RALPH SUBAGENT] Subagent completed but did not merge or kick back. Review required.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"todos\": [],\n  \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-semantic-exit-codes\",\n      \"title\": \"Semantic Exit Codes\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"when\": \"operation succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 0\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"user input is invalid\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"command is cancelled by user\",\n          \"when\": \"confirmation prompt declined\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters runtime error\",\n          \"when\": \"operation fails during execution\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"command finds nothing\",\n          \"when\": \"query returns no results\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 0 with empty result set\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command used incorrectly\",\n          \"when\": \"invalid flags or arguments provided\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1 with usage information\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"batch operation completes\",\n          \"when\": \"partial failures occur\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command documentation\",\n          \"when\": \"developers implement commands\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code meanings documented in code\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-dry-run\",\n      \"title\": \"Dry Run Preview Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports dry run\",\n          \"when\": \"--dry-run flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"show what would be changed without applying\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes\",\n          \"then\": \"no files are modified\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"output is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"clear indication that this is a preview\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command would error\",\n          \"then\": \"error shown but no state changed\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"--dry-run and --force both provided\",\n          \"when\": \"command executes\",\n          \"then\": \"dry run takes precedence (no changes made)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--dry-run --json provided\",\n          \"then\": \"JSON output includes dry_run boolean field\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1513YJA4PKRTA8CZDE4P\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"kspec task set --priority accepts numbers (1-5) but all documentation, conventions, and plan documen\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"**What**: `kspec task set --priority` and `kspec task add --priority` only accept raw numbers (1-5), but all documentation, conventions, and plan documents use P1/P2/P3 notation. The error message says 'Priority must be a number between 1 and 5' which is confusing when P-notation is used everywhere else. **Where**: `src/cli/validators.ts` — the `parseIntOption()` function (line 36-64) is used for priority parsing. It calls `Number(value)` which rejects `P1` etc. The priority option is defined in `src/cli/commands/task.ts` at lines 608, 827. The `parseIntOption` is called at lines 287-296 (task set) and 759-767 (task add). **How**: Create a `parsePriority()` wrapper function in `src/cli/validators.ts` that first normalizes P-notation before calling `parseIntOption()`. Implementation: strip a leading case-insensitive `P` prefix if present (`value.replace(/^[Pp]/, '')`), then delegate to `parseIntOption()`. Replace all `parseIntOption(options.priority, { min: 1, max: 5, name: 'Priority' })` calls in `task.ts` with `parsePriority(options.priority)`. Update the option description from 'Priority (1-5)' to 'Priority (1-5 or P1-P5)'. Update the error message to mention both formats. **Done when**: (1) `kspec task set @ref --priority P1` works and sets priority to 1. (2) `kspec task add --priority p3` works (case-insensitive). (3) `kspec task set @ref --priority 2` still works (backward compatible). (4) Invalid values like `P6`, `Px`, `0` are rejected with a clear error mentioning both formats. (5) Tests in `tests/cli-validators.test.ts` cover both formats. (6) CLI help text shows accepted format.\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@batch-exec\",\n  \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n  